+++ b/CORE-MIGRATION-REHEARSAL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Core migration candidate — not for deployment
+
+This isolated site candidate consumes the selected unpublished contrast-corrected core tarball and the matching private Astro 2.0.0 candidate. `package-lock.json` resolves the checked-in fixtures for reproducible local `npm ci`; the manifests retain their intended exact semver. This is a rehearsal lock, not evidence that either package exists on npm. Replace fixture resolutions with independently verified registry integrity after separately approved publication. Historical `/theme` installation guidance and source-shell provenance remain public-release records.
+
+Full builds accept `DESIGN_REACT_ARCHIVE` pointing at the existing SHA-256-pinned React reference archive; the unchanged fetch script validates the archive and provenance before extraction. `SITE_BASE` selects `/` or a subpath. The build rebases only the generated copy of that archive's assets; it leaves the pinned source archive unchanged. The source Markdown copies are also unchanged; an HTML transformation resolves their assembled-page link and duplicate heading ID.
+
+The site-owned static pages passed root and `/preview` link verification. Chromium passed both base paths including the browser-rendered React reference and local assets; the static verifier's requirement for an HTML `h1` is inapplicable to the client-rendered reference, which is checked after rendering. Firefox and WebKit remain to be verified. Build-generated tracked agent archives must not be inadvertently committed.
+
+Do not deploy this candidate. GitHub Actions are verification-only, but external Cloudflare preview triggers have not been enumerated; do not push a site branch or create a site PR until their behavior is verified or a separately authorized safe route is provided. Site adoption and deployment require separate approval. Public download and generated agent records need a coordinated post-publication review.
